<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abd Allah ibn al-Aftas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1022–1045</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abd <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allah">Allah</a> ibn al-Aftas, of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berber</a> descent, was the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aftasid-dynasty">Aftasid dynasty</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">Taifa</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badajoz">Badajoz</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">Vizier</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabur-al-saqlabi">Sabur al-Saqlabi</a>, ruler of the old Lower March around Mérida and Badajoz, he seized power after Sabur's death in 1022 and ruled until about 1045, fighting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbadid-dynasty">Abbadids</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a>. His successors added <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/evora">Évora</a> and ruled until the Almoravid conquest of 1094.</p></div>
